.TH CHTTPSVR_RESP_PRINTF 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_resp_printf \- format and append a printf-style string to the response body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_resp_printf(chttpsvr_resp *resp,
                                    const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Formats fmt and the variadic arguments under the printf rules, then
appends the result to the response body.  This is the same as a format
into a temporary string and then a call to chttpsvr_resp_write_str
with it.  The function uses a small internal stack buffer for short
output.  For longer output it falls back to a temporary heap
allocation, and it frees that allocation before it returns.  That
allocation has exactly the size of the formatted text.  More than one
call adds to the same response body, in the same way as
chttpsvr_resp_write_str.

The compiler checks the format string with the GCC attribute
__attribute__((format(printf, 2, 3))).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - The function appended the formatted output to
                         the body.
ccol_invalid_args      - resp or fmt is NULL, or the vsnprintf call
                          under it reports an encoding error.
ccol_not_enough_memory - The library could not allocate the body
                          buffer or the temporary heap buffer.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write_str (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write_json (3)
